.TH ENV "1" "April 2026" "PiggyOS" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
env \- print environment variables, or run a program in a modified environment

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B env
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... [\fI\,-\/\fR] [\fI\,NAME=VALUE\/\fR]... [\fI\,COMMAND \/\fR[\fI\,ARG\/\fR]...]

.SH DESCRIPTION

.PP
Set each NAME environment variable to VALUE and run COMMAND. If no COMMAND is specified, print the resulting environment.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.B \-0
end each output line with NUL, not newline

.TP
.B \-C DIR
change working directory to DIR

.TP
.B \-a ARG
pass ARG as the zeroth argument of COMMAND

.TP
.B \-i
start with empty environment

.TP
.B \-u NAME
remove variable NAME from the environment

